    "body": "Depends on: #64 and the cover fineness sweep. The PDF's original double-counting mitigation expects interaction residuals attached to canonical overlap nodes when overlapping memberships carry non-independent evidence. The induced cover currently has no explicit overlap nodes (only E_o edges). Evaluate whether any high-co-activation region pairs (from the E_o builder) justify materializing an overlap node with an interaction residual ΔI(pair,v) = lnP(v|pair) − lnP(v|p1) − lnP(v|p2) + lnP(v|parent), gated on held-out gain vs its bytes. Acceptance: overlap nodes exist only where the held-out bits/token improvement exceeds a documented threshold (else this issue closes as 'evaluated, not justified' with the numbers).\n\n\n---\n\n## Definition of Done\n- A principled evaluation decides whether any high-co-activation region pairs justify explicit overlap nodes with interaction residuals.\n- Overlap nodes exist in artifacts only where held-out gain exceeds the documented byte threshold — or the candidate is closed as evaluated-and-rejected with numbers.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n- [ ] Candidate pairs are selected by a documented co-activation criterion (not hand-picked).\n- [ ] Per-candidate held-out bits/token delta vs artifact bytes is reported.\n- [ ] If adopted: Theorem 10 non-duplication tests cover interaction entries (unique canonical contribution IDs).\n- [ ] If rejected: the measured table proving non-justification is attached.",
